WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.520
Hi! I'm Georgina from BBC Learning English.

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:06.720
In today's lesson, we're looking at mixed conditionals.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:08.900
We usually use mixed conditionals

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.220
to talk about a past imaginary situation

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:15.540
that has a present imaginary result.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:16.580
For example:

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:20.000
If I had eaten breakfast, I wouldn't be hungry now.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.200
The first phrase

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:25.180
uses the same structure as the third conditional

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:27.880
– if + past perfect.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:31.200
This is because it is a past imaginary situation.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.580
It's not true. I didn't eat breakfast.

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:35.760
The second phrase

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:39.680
uses the same structure as the second conditional

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:43.180
– would + infinitive (no to).

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:47.700
This is because it is a present imaginary result.

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:52.380
It's not true. I am hungry because I didn't eat breakfast.

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:55.720
Don't forget to put the comma in after the 'if' clause.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:56.680
Bye for now!

